WEBVTT

01:24.060 --> 01:29.980
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

01:49.380 --> 01:54.930
<i>She's always by herself, 
gazing at the people who visit the park.</i>

02:03.890 --> 02:09.340
<i>You can only see her for a short time, 
while the cherry tree is in bloom.</i>

02:17.250 --> 02:19.830
<i>Wh-Who's that old guy?!</i>

02:21.240 --> 02:23.240
<i>He's talking with her...</i>

02:40.190 --> 02:41.940
Hey, old dude!

02:41.940 --> 02:42.900
What?

03:02.620 --> 03:06.120
Old dude, you get to talk with 
the cherry blossom girl?

03:06.450 --> 03:07.400
Huh?

03:07.400 --> 03:11.240
I don't know where you came from, kid, 
but don't go throwing sticks at—

03:11.240 --> 03:11.860
Here!

03:12.730 --> 03:15.410
Give this to her!

03:16.520 --> 03:18.680
What's this clod supposed to be?

03:18.680 --> 03:20.230
A triangle!

03:20.230 --> 03:22.290
She likes triangles, doesn't she?

03:22.290 --> 03:23.420
I was watching.

03:42.140 --> 03:43.310
How'd it go?

03:43.310 --> 03:45.650
Do it yourself next time, brat.

03:45.650 --> 03:46.720
Did she like it?!

03:46.720 --> 03:48.860
Listen when I'm talking.

03:50.030 --> 03:52.270
Though I suppose she was pleased.

03:52.270 --> 03:53.330
Really?!

03:53.330 --> 03:54.640
She was also puzzled.

03:57.410 --> 03:59.760
<i>While the cherry tree's in full bloom,</i>

04:00.510 --> 04:04.880
<i>I've gotten a smidge closer to her 
thanks to this old guy who stopped by.</i>

04:16.710 --> 04:18.010
Oh, hey, old dude!

04:18.010 --> 04:20.150
At least call me "mister."

04:20.150 --> 04:24.160
You're always here, brat. 
You <i>do</i> go home, don't you?

04:25.120 --> 04:29.380
Also, stop mass-producing 
these inedible triangles.

04:29.380 --> 04:31.320
What's an edible triangle?

04:34.360 --> 04:35.340
Use this.

04:35.650 --> 04:39.380
This is the last time I'm helping you, got it?

04:40.130 --> 04:41.320
What's this?

04:41.320 --> 04:42.630
A string telephone.

04:42.630 --> 04:43.660
String...?

04:45.350 --> 04:46.700
Hello.

04:47.670 --> 04:51.110
Thank you for all the triangles.

04:53.710 --> 04:55.600
Hello?

04:56.430 --> 05:00.240
<i>This is the first time
I've heard her voice...</i>

05:06.270 --> 05:08.830
<i>It's almost time for the 
cherry blossoms to scatter.</i>

05:08.830 --> 05:11.610
<i>And I won't be here much longer either.</i>

05:13.110 --> 05:14.110
Uh...

05:14.760 --> 05:15.690
I've...

05:16.590 --> 05:18.920
been watching you all this time.

05:18.920 --> 05:21.630
I still don't know you at all...

05:22.670 --> 05:23.810
but listen!

05:34.700 --> 05:37.760
<i>I said that was the last time I'd help,</i>

05:38.180 --> 05:40.310
<i>so I'm just seeing how things play out.</i>

05:45.550 --> 05:48.200
<i>The tree where I always saw him is gone.</i>

06:13.570 --> 06:18.270
Even if I say hello, 
I no longer hear anything.

06:18.650 --> 06:22.030
They took him out of the ground
and took him away.

06:22.960 --> 06:25.270
He said he's going to become a promenade.

06:26.600 --> 06:27.980
I miss him.

06:30.040 --> 06:33.420
Even if I bloom next year, 
I'll never see him again.

07:05.580 --> 07:07.860
The cherry blossoms have fallen already.

07:07.860 --> 07:09.820
Wasn't that one kinda early?

07:09.820 --> 07:11.490
Hey, that bench is new!

07:11.490 --> 07:12.590
You're right!

07:14.420 --> 07:15.370
Huh?

07:15.950 --> 07:16.970
My...

07:18.090 --> 07:21.870
My body's become a people seat.

07:23.870 --> 07:25.490
<i>That's her tree!</i>

07:25.490 --> 07:26.710
Is that you, brat?

07:29.120 --> 07:31.060
What're you doing here, old dude?

07:31.060 --> 07:32.470
That's my line.

07:32.470 --> 07:34.960
Looks like I'm this seat now.

07:35.530 --> 07:37.250
Where is she, though?

07:37.250 --> 07:38.280
Who?

07:38.280 --> 07:39.390
The cherry tree girl.

07:39.390 --> 07:41.310
She already scattered.

07:41.310 --> 07:42.810
Oh.

07:42.810 --> 07:45.020
Too bad I didn't get here a bit sooner.

07:47.890 --> 07:49.710
Wow, cool.

07:49.710 --> 07:51.320
I can go right up to it.

07:51.320 --> 07:53.900
There's no telling if it'll bloom next year.

07:55.450 --> 07:57.190
That's okay.

07:58.330 --> 08:01.480
Before, all I could do was watch.

08:01.480 --> 08:05.830
But I got to hear her voice,
and even though I look different now,

08:05.830 --> 08:07.930
look how close I am!

08:08.800 --> 08:10.270
I'll just keep waiting...

08:11.130 --> 08:13.520
until a spring comes when she blossoms.

08:19.010 --> 08:25.020
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

08:19.010 --> 08:25.020
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

08:45.390 --> 08:48.540
<i>Is that a kitty I hear?</i>

08:48.890 --> 08:53.660
<i>What if it's out here freezing in this rain?</i>

08:57.960 --> 08:59.970
Kitty...

09:02.270 --> 09:03.380
Kitty!

09:07.940 --> 09:10.190
<b>Please adopt me</b>

09:10.970 --> 09:13.520
<i>This isn't what I was expecting.</i>

09:16.030 --> 09:19.810
<i>It's modeled after a kitty, 
but it's not a kitty.</i>

09:20.310 --> 09:21.530
<i>Must be a robot.</i>

09:24.280 --> 09:25.930
<i>Is it from Earth?</i>

09:25.930 --> 09:28.540
<i>No, maybe some other planet?</i>

09:33.070 --> 09:34.550
Human...

09:34.830 --> 09:36.600
<i>It spoke.</i>

09:36.600 --> 09:38.830
<i>And it referred to me as a human.</i>

09:38.830 --> 09:42.050
<i>Something tells me I shouldn't get involved.</i>

10:45.820 --> 10:49.830
Human... what are you... doing here?

10:49.830 --> 10:51.590
Just passing through.

10:51.590 --> 10:54.070
What the heck are <i>you</i> doing here?

10:54.810 --> 10:58.850
Do I... look like I'm... doing something?

10:58.850 --> 11:03.730
I'm just... waiting for my...
 energy to run out.

11:04.960 --> 11:06.220
I see.

11:07.240 --> 11:08.740
Sorry to bother you.

11:09.680 --> 11:10.540
Hey.

11:12.210 --> 11:13.240
This.

11:14.380 --> 11:17.490
It'll rain again tomorrow. 
Feel free to use it.

11:28.970 --> 11:32.240
Experiment C-018 is to be discarded.

11:39.500 --> 11:41.050
<i>Discarded?</i>

11:42.480 --> 11:44.260
<i>Abandoned...?</i>

11:50.940 --> 11:55.180
<i>If I could defeat at least one human...</i>

11:56.430 --> 11:57.860
<i>Human...</i>

12:06.250 --> 12:08.200
What are you here for this time?!

12:08.200 --> 12:09.820
You make it sound so horrible.

12:10.130 --> 12:12.490
I just hooked you up to this battery.

12:13.490 --> 12:15.510
I can move now.

12:17.380 --> 12:18.690
<i>Human...</i>

12:20.060 --> 12:21.450
<i>That's right.</i>

12:22.180 --> 12:23.450
Human!

12:28.710 --> 12:30.880
That's where your mouth is?

12:31.750 --> 12:32.920
Nothing's coming out.

12:32.920 --> 12:34.210
Wh-Why not?

12:34.210 --> 12:35.430
<i>I'll do it again!</i>

12:38.840 --> 12:39.790
Hey.

12:40.710 --> 12:43.920
<i>Experiment C-018 is to be discarded.</i>

12:42.820 --> 12:44.490
Discarded

12:48.160 --> 12:52.240
<i>I really am useless...</i>

13:03.730 --> 13:05.040
What's this?

13:04.010 --> 13:05.510
<b>Cat Food</b>

13:05.520 --> 13:06.970
It's cat food.

13:06.970 --> 13:10.080
Didn't you bite me before 
because you were hungry?

13:10.080 --> 13:11.430
Not even close!

13:11.430 --> 13:15.910
Besides, C-018 cannot ingest food!

13:16.400 --> 13:17.760
I see.

13:18.070 --> 13:23.650
What are you up to, trying to win me over?!

13:24.210 --> 13:26.300
What am I "up to"?

13:27.100 --> 13:32.780
I'd feel pretty guilty just standing by and 
watching something modeled after a kitty die.

13:36.250 --> 13:39.340
I wouldn't mind thanking you 
for the umbrella and battery.

13:39.340 --> 13:40.080
Huh?

13:40.540 --> 13:43.380
If you don't want to, that's fine.

13:49.670 --> 13:53.720
<i>It's smooth instead of fluffy.</i>

13:55.930 --> 14:01.940
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

13:55.930 --> 14:01.940
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

14:11.070 --> 14:13.220
I'd like to ask you a favor, General.

14:16.250 --> 14:18.290
A few hours ago

14:17.110 --> 14:21.220
If you encounter a suspicious object that
doesn't seem to be from our planet or Earth,

14:21.220 --> 14:22.890
could you let me know?

14:22.890 --> 14:25.260
Huh? What's this about?

14:26.310 --> 14:30.900
It looks like we aren't 
the only outsiders targeting Earth.

14:30.900 --> 14:34.440
Our competition might be developing weaponry.

14:34.930 --> 14:38.320
It's possible they've already 
sent some to Earth.

14:38.730 --> 14:41.870
Why didn't you mention this earlier 
at the executive meeting?

14:43.190 --> 14:47.060
I still don't have enough 
evidence for a report.

14:47.060 --> 14:50.690
It's really nothing more 
than a remote possibility.

14:51.090 --> 14:53.090
How is this a favor?

14:53.090 --> 14:55.120
More like additional work.

14:55.120 --> 14:57.560
You'll do it, General?!

14:57.560 --> 15:03.880
However, if I find anything outside working 
hours, I'm treating it as overtime.

15:04.920 --> 15:06.830
Of course, General!

15:14.310 --> 15:15.940
<i>It's this thing.</i>

15:16.310 --> 15:21.440
<i>When Rooney told me, I wasn't 
thinking it would be a robot weapon.</i>

15:21.440 --> 15:24.940
<i>But any way you look at it, 
this has gotta be the weapon.</i>

15:25.430 --> 15:29.440
<i>It said it didn't bite me out of hunger,</i>

15:29.900 --> 15:35.190
<i>meaning there's a good chance something 
was loaded into those fang-shaped spikes.</i>

15:35.190 --> 15:37.450
<i>Even if it's not all that dangerous,</i>

15:37.450 --> 15:40.940
<i>I </i>should<i> take it back to HQ as a specimen.</i>

15:46.060 --> 15:48.460
All done charging?

15:48.750 --> 15:49.770
All done.

15:57.390 --> 15:58.630
You unplugged it!

15:58.630 --> 16:03.240
Nobody asked you! I can do it myself!

16:03.240 --> 16:06.480
What the hell're you saying? 
You couldn't reach it.

16:08.930 --> 16:10.980
<i>This is what I get for being nice.</i>

16:25.620 --> 16:26.790
<i>Now what?</i>

16:27.260 --> 16:30.300
<i>Could it be preparing for some attack?</i>

16:30.300 --> 16:32.260
<i>I should just hurry and take it to—</i>

16:32.260 --> 16:32.900
Hey.

16:36.100 --> 16:38.260
You're not going to pet me?

16:41.060 --> 16:46.690
He didn't see any harm

16:41.860 --> 16:46.380
<i>Maybe it's not a weapon, 
but an extraterrestrial robot pet?</i>

16:46.680 --> 16:51.060
<i>Well, it might not be dangerous, 
but I have a job to do.</i>

16:51.060 --> 16:52.050
Hey.

16:53.750 --> 16:56.310
Care to take a walk with me?

16:56.820 --> 17:00.160
I guess I'll have to, if you insist.

17:01.710 --> 17:06.290
<i>Not only did I notify Rooney, 
I brought it to headquarters...</i>

17:07.150 --> 17:08.420
You...

17:09.540 --> 17:12.290
You're from another planet?

17:13.210 --> 17:16.830
I don't recall ever saying 
I was an Earthling.

17:18.300 --> 17:20.310
<b>Silence...</b>

17:20.820 --> 17:26.440
Sorry this turned into me deceiving you,
 but I have my own job to do.

17:27.000 --> 17:30.060
This should be a simple inspection, 
and you'll soon be back—

17:30.150 --> 17:31.570
<b>SENSE OF GUILT</b>

17:31.570 --> 17:32.790
Hey!

17:33.870 --> 17:36.320
General, you brought it in!

17:36.600 --> 17:38.710
You always do such quick work.

17:38.710 --> 17:40.450
Thank you. I know it was dangerous.

17:40.450 --> 17:43.730
I told you the threat level was low.

17:43.730 --> 17:47.910
I know, but we can't be certain
 until we examine it.

17:49.770 --> 17:52.840
Yes, that form <i>would</i> make many 
Earthlings lower their guard.

17:52.840 --> 17:54.950
Rooney, will this—

17:54.950 --> 17:57.570
Okay, you can leave it in our hands.

17:57.570 --> 17:58.720
I'll call when we're done!

17:58.720 --> 17:59.220
Hey!

17:59.220 --> 18:00.420
Hey, listen!

18:00.420 --> 18:02.120
Tell me later, General!

18:03.430 --> 18:05.180
<b>SENSE OF GUILT</b>

18:07.690 --> 18:10.440
<b>15 minutes later</b>

18:10.440 --> 18:12.690
<b>30 minutes later</b>

18:12.690 --> 18:14.690
<b>45 minutes later</b>

18:14.680 --> 18:17.250
What's the matter with the General?

18:14.690 --> 18:23.540
<b>1 hour later</b>

18:17.250 --> 18:20.850
I hear Rooney is investigating 
some alien weapon.

18:20.850 --> 18:23.530
Aha, the General must be on alert.

18:34.080 --> 18:37.010
Hey, Rooney, how much longer will it take?

18:37.280 --> 18:38.760
<i>General?</i>

18:38.760 --> 18:40.380
<i>You're so impatient.</i>

18:41.750 --> 18:44.130
<i>I think I'd like two more hours.</i>

18:53.370 --> 18:54.870
All right...

18:54.870 --> 18:57.990
<i>No need to be so worried. I'm fine.</i>

18:57.990 --> 19:00.290
I'm not worried about you.

19:00.290 --> 19:01.940
<i>There you go again!</i>

19:01.940 --> 19:05.460
<i>But hey, like you said, 
it doesn't appear to be dangerous.</i>

19:06.030 --> 19:07.520
<i>Welp, gotta get back to it!</i>

19:07.520 --> 19:08.360
Yeah.

19:14.570 --> 19:15.960
Excuse me, sir.

19:17.580 --> 19:19.060
I'd like to ask you something.

19:19.540 --> 19:20.600
Sure.

19:37.040 --> 19:39.640
<i>General? Hello?</i>

19:40.360 --> 19:43.210
<i>General, can you hear me?</i>

19:43.210 --> 19:44.860
I wasn't listening.

19:45.240 --> 19:46.710
<i>Come on.</i>

19:46.710 --> 19:50.150
<i>I asked you to drop by because 
I'm done with the investigation.</i>

19:57.100 --> 20:02.550
<i>Surprisingly, I might have developed 
an attachment to that robot.</i>

20:03.650 --> 20:06.880
<i>I knew dismantlement was a possibility.</i>

20:06.880 --> 20:10.330
<i>A necessary sacrifice for our home world.</i>

20:17.440 --> 20:19.220
Oh, General!

20:24.590 --> 20:28.900
As soon as I reassembled this little guy,
 it started freaking out.

20:28.900 --> 20:30.510
Can I take it apart again?

20:30.510 --> 20:32.000
I may have screwed up somehow.

20:32.000 --> 20:34.000
No! Stop it!

20:36.860 --> 20:41.890
This guy tricked C-018,
 but he's still better than you!

20:42.180 --> 20:45.490
Don't be mean.
I'm the one who cleaned you up.

20:47.410 --> 20:49.150
What are you talking about?

20:49.560 --> 20:56.110
I checked out all its parts and features,
plus cleaned what was dirty.

20:58.080 --> 21:01.450
We got all the data we needed, of course,

21:01.830 --> 21:06.510
and upon concluding that it poses 
no danger, we reassembled it.

21:07.440 --> 21:10.610
Why was the dismembered head just lying there?

21:10.610 --> 21:13.510
I was doing an internal check 
while cleaning the joints.

21:13.510 --> 21:15.030
They get dirty easily.

21:15.940 --> 21:18.620
That's a damned misleading thing to do.

21:18.620 --> 21:20.710
Huh? Why're you mad?

21:21.210 --> 21:23.480
What happens to it now?

21:25.480 --> 21:30.220
That depends what the executive council 
decides, but it's practically a robot pet.

21:31.010 --> 21:32.520
<i>I knew it.</i>

21:32.520 --> 21:35.230
We could keep an eye on it at HQ.

21:35.510 --> 21:37.490
But it seems to like you.

21:38.080 --> 21:42.780
I think another option would be 
for you to look after it at your place.

21:43.110 --> 21:44.440
What say you?

23:20.000 --> 23:20.710
MR. VILLAIN'S DAY OFF

23:20.000 --> 23:20.710
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

23:22.490 --> 23:29.140
The evergreen oak boy 
and cherry tree girl meet up.

23:29.640 --> 23:32.560
A dream while fast asleep.

23:32.900 --> 23:35.380
Recollections that stir up.

23:36.580 --> 23:40.820
Hide-and-seek, until we meet again someday.

23:42.890 --> 23:45.650
A sentimental weekend.

23:46.180 --> 23:48.640
Somewhere on this planet.

23:48.650 --> 23:49.940
Somewhere on This Planet
